 :sections
 [{:id     "about"
   :title  "What clogem-press is"
   :blocks [[:p "clogem-press builds a static website from a folder of Markdown files: a knowledge base, a blog, documentation, or all three in one site. It follows the content conventions of "
             [:a "https://github.com/xugaoyi/vuepress-theme-vdoing" "vuepress-theme-vdoing"]
             ": numbered folders become the sidebar, front matter is written for you, and every article gets a short permanent address."]
            [:p "It runs on " [:a "https://babashka.org/" "babashka"]
             ", with no library to install: Markdown, templates, YAML, HTTP and feeds all come built into babashka."]
            [:p "One site can hold up to five languages: English, Simplified and Traditional Chinese, Malay and Tamil. An article's versions share one address, so a reader can switch between them."]]}

  {:id     "status"
   :title  "What it does today"
   :blocks [[:p "The latest release is " [:strong "0.2.0"] ". Work on the next phase is in progress on the main branch and is not released yet. The "
             [:a "https://github.com/EchoJustus/clogem-press/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" "changelog"]
             " lists every change as it lands."]
            [:cards
             {:chip  "Released · 0.2.0"
              :title "Content and structure"
              :text  ["A sidebar from numbered folders, front matter written for you with stable permanent links, category, tag and archive pages, a paginated blog home with pinned posts, breadcrumbs, previous and next links, catalogue pages and Markdown containers."]}
             {:chip  "Released · 0.2.0"
              :title "Languages and discovery"
              :text  ["Five languages with one address per article, canonical and hreflang links, an Atom feed per language, a sitemap, Pagefind search with an index per language, and optional giscus comments with one thread per article."]}
             {:chip  "In progress · unreleased"
              :title "The theme, on the main branch"
              :text  ["Landed so far: light, dark and reading colour modes, code highlighting, a live-reloading " [:code "bb dev"]
                      ", card and line page styles, a navbar with a mobile drawer, edit links and last-updated dates, a 404 page, the blog's profile card and home banner, and optional analytics and search-console tags. Still to come in this phase: custom HTML slots and search across languages, then the next release."]}]]}

  {:id     "start"
   :title  "Getting started"
   :blocks [[:p "You need " [:a "https://babashka.org/" "babashka"] " 1.13.219 or newer, and git. clogem-press runs from your site's folder against a copy of the generator beside it:"]
            [:pre "git clone https://github.com/EchoJustus/clogem-press\ncd my-site\nbb --config ../clogem-press/bb.edn dev      # build, serve on localhost:1888, rebuild on change\nbb --config ../clogem-press/bb.edn build    # write the site to dist/\nbb --config ../clogem-press/bb.edn doctor   # report content problems without building"]
            [:ul
             [[:a "https://github.com/EchoJustus/clogem-press#readme" "The README"] ": every task and option, the conventions on one screen, and the theme's settings."]
             [[:a "https://github.com/EchoJustus/clogem-press/tree/main/examples/demo-site" "The demo site"] ": a complete site to copy from, which the tests build on every change."]
             [[:a "https://github.com/EchoJustus/clogem-press/blob/main/config.example.edn" "config.example.edn"] ": every setting with its default."]
             [[:a "https://github.com/EchoJustus/clogem-press/blob/main/DESIGN.md" "DESIGN.md"] ": the design and the reasons behind it."]]]}

